From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 15:55:57 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 138/139] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali: Mark the USB3-DP PHY as
 a Type-C mode switch

The QMP USB3-DP combo PHY switches between USB3 + 2-lane DP and 4-lane
DP from the Type-C mux state, but on Kaanapali it only receives the
orientation. Without "mode-switch" the PHY stays in USB3 + DP mode and
DisplayPort is limited to two lanes even when the sink uses pin
assignment C. SM8750, the closest relative, already has the property.

Signed-off-by: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
index 11c313b83..fcf02b1b5 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
@@ -3736,6 +3736,7 @@ usb_dp_qmpphy: phy@88e8000 {
 			#clock-cells = <1>;
 			#phy-cells = <1>;
 
+			mode-switch;
 			orientation-switch;
 
 			status = "disabled";
-- 
